      "14444741": {
        "id": 14444741,
        "created_at": "Jul 5 2024",
        "updated_at": "Aug 13 2026",
        "rating": 10,
        "review": "HOLY SHIT. This is the first time since like, Sekiro/Elden Ring/Persona 5 Royal that all I can think about is to play a game. 10/10, 25 hours and still only in Act 1 doing so many quests. The voice-acting, the dnd gameplay, everything (besides the inventory management bc its meh), perfection. THE MUSIC. Looking forward to my Honor Mode playthorugh, can't wait to replay this so much with different play-styles and get the different endings :D. EDIT: After beating the game I will say, it doesn't \"fall off\" in act 3 but it does fill a bit rushed and bugs are a little more prominent in act 3. However, does that take away from this absolute masterpiece of a game? No, not in the slightest (mostly). \n\nI will try to not spoil anything here but that epilogue with Karlach and Wyll when you finish all their quests. \n\nShadowhearts epligoue. AND WITHERS. Astarion and La'zel and Gale all won me over by the end of the game, and Halsin, you gorgeous man, I wish I didn't have to turn you down but I will do your romance in a future play through I promise.\n\nThese characters show, well, character, they have personalities that shift and change and evolve (hehe the emperor would be proud), and some are redeemable and savable, some are not. The first game/story (besides Persona), that has made me genuinely care for the characters in such a connected way. I don't want to compare the two games/series in anyway to be fully clear, but these characters, their flaws and their ambitions and selfishness and selflessness. THE HOUSE OF HOPE'S THEME. Betrayal, lies, deception and comradery, it has it all. It makes the game shine and I would not have it any other way. \n\nIt is absolutely gonna break my heart when I do the evil/bad play through because I go into it with the knowledge of how I could have potentially helped so many of these characters, but I want to check out Mizora, and Raphael, and Minthara. I want to see how those characters evolve and showcase their prowess and selfishness. And finally, yes, I am so looking forward to the dark urge playthrough, not just for the \"special ending\", but to hopefully do a honor mode dark urge redemption playthrough, and explore hopefully everything that I missed in my first playthrough. \n\nDOWN DOWN DOWN BY THE RIVER - BANGER 10/10 WHEN IT PLAYS DURING THE CREDIT SCENE, so so so good.",
